  "methodology": [
    "Four sequential samples per comparison on the same already-Available Codespace, using ABBA method order. Existing image caches and saved application data were retained.",
    "Both use the actual production bootstrap with its nohup runner launch removed. They verify the identical runner SHA and discover Node; the downloaded runner is never executed and no application is started.",
    "In the overlap comparison, the SSH child starts with its stdin open and empty while the ordinary private-port lookup runs. The harmless probe script is written only after the target port is confirmed private.",
    "The SSH command must finish successfully. Each script creates an isolated temporary directory and installs an EXIT cleanup trap. No application cache, database, volume or existing file is cleared.",
    "The local provider-state API read and fetching the public runner once on aswin are setup, excluded from these command timings."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Two samples per method, one environment and sequential scheduling do not establish a guaranteed speedup. First download timings differ materially from the later download.",
    "The production launch sequence is still sequential; overlapping transport remains a candidate requiring cancellation, deadline, retry, privacy-gate tests and real application acceptance.",
    "These command probes do not measure application startup, first-image delivery, browser product visibility or cold compute.",
    "The archived scripts are the exact aswin-specific reproducers used. They target the named authorized test Codespace and accept its GitHub token only through stdin."
  ],
  "decision": "Prioritize overlapping SSH connection establishment with private preview verification, while holding bootstrap bytes until privacy is confirmed. Inline runner transfer showed a smaller and more variable saving; leave production runner delivery unchanged for now.",
